import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---
<PageLayout title="Colophon" eyebrow="A peek behind the leaves" intro="A few notes about how this website is made, and the things it tries to care about.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Made to be small</h2><p>Built with <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a>, written in Markdown, and served as static pages. No trackers, no third-party fonts, and no account needed. An <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> lets you follow new writing on your own terms.</p>
    <h2>Type & little details</h2><p>Headings are set in <a href="https://github.com/subframe7536/maple-font">Maple Mono</a>, paired with <a href="https://github.com/googlefonts/dm-fonts">DM Sans</a> for the body. The little icons come from <a href="https://phosphoricons.com/">Phosphor</a>.</p>
    <p>The <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Exeter_College_Oxford_Coat_Of_Arms.svg">Exeter College coat of arms</a> is by ChevronTango, shared under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/">CC BY-SA 3.0</a> and resized for this site.</p>
    <h2>A comfortable visit</h2><p>The site follows your device's light or dark preference, with a little sun-and-moon dial if you want to change it. Motion takes a rest when your device asks for reduced animation. The words and links work with JavaScript switched off, too.</p>
    <h2>Seeds of inspiration</h2><p>The quiet, personal homepage of <a href="https://pedromarques.me/">Pedro Marques</a> and the independent-web spirit of <a href="https://brennan.day/">Brennan's website</a> helped inspire this space.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
